# Copy to `.env.production` (same folder, gitignored) and fill in your
# REAL production values before the first deploy.
#
# Why this file exists: frontend-admin/.env (committed, tracked in git)
# holds LOCAL DEV values (http://admin.localhost:8010) — see that
# file's own comments for why. Vite loads `.env.production` on top of
# `.env` for any `vite build` (mode=production, which is what
# `npm run build` and scripts/deploy.sh both use), so without a real
# `.env.production` here, a production build would silently embed the
# dev "admin.localhost" API URL — the site would load but every API
# call would fail. deploy.sh checks this file exists before building,
# specifically to catch that.

# The backend's real public URL — the subdomain you pointed at
# backend/public in Hostinger (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §3-4).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com
